<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Warsaw (1920)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Miracle on the Vistula · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-soviet-war">Polish–Soviet War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a> was fought in August 1920 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-soviet-war">Polish–Soviet War</a>, when Polish forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jozef-pilsudski">Józef Piłsudski</a> counter-attacked the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> advancing on the Polish capital. The Soviet armies under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mikhail-tukhachevsky">Mikhail Tukhachevsky</a> were routed and driven back. The victory, called the 'Miracle on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>', preserved Polish independence and led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-riga">Peace of Riga</a> in 1921.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-warsaw-1920.jpg" alt="Battle of Warsaw (1920)" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: patrickgom0 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Warsaw_1920.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
